# Keep build contexts lean and deterministic: dependencies are installed
# inside the image from the lockfile, never copied from the host — and no
# locally generated artifact may enter a layer. `out` matters beyond size:
# generation outputs and the worker's failed-generation dumps (cwd-relative
# `out/`, e.g. apps/worker/out) carry private PR/code context.
.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.output
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
out
**/out
build
**/build
coverage
**/coverage
docs
# Local-only output and other checkouts, never part of a release: the image
# a developer builds must match the one CI builds from a clean checkout.
# Patterns here anchor at the context root, unlike .gitignore, so every
# entry carries `**/`. Instance config is mounted, not baked (see the
# compose files).
**/mergebrief.config.yaml
**/logs
**/*.log
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.playwright-cli
**/.screenshots
**/.artifacts
**/.worktrees
**/.pnpm-store
**/.claude
**/.serena
**/eval-reports
**/*.cert
# Mirror .gitignore's secret patterns — nothing credential-shaped may enter
# an image layer (COPY . . would otherwise bake it in).
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
secrets
